def determine_action(pole_angle, pole_velocity, cart_position, cart_velocity):
    # Dynamic threshold calculation based on current velocities
    angle_threshold = max(0.01, abs(pole_velocity) * 0.5)
    position_threshold = max(0.1, abs(cart_velocity) * 0.2)

    # Proportional control for actions
    if abs(pole_angle) > angle_threshold:
        if pole_angle > 0 and cart_position < position_threshold:
            return 2  # Push right to correct positive angle
        elif pole_angle < 0 and cart_position > -position_threshold:
            return 1  # Push left to correct negative angle
    if abs(cart_position) > position_threshold:
        if cart_position > 0 and pole_velocity < angle_threshold:
            return 2  # Push right to correct positive position
        elif cart_position < 0 and pole_velocity > -angle_threshold:
            return 1  # Push left to correct negative position
    if abs(pole_velocity) > angle_threshold or abs(cart_velocity) > position_threshold:
        if pole_velocity > 0:
            return 2  # Push right to counteract positive velocity
        elif pole_velocity < 0:
            return 1  # Push left to counteract negative velocity
    else:
        return 1  # Default action to maintain stability
```

### Conclusion
The updated strategy incorporates dynamic thresholds, considers both position and velocity, and applies proportional control. This should make the cart-pole system more responsive and effective in maintaining balance for longer periods. Implementing this strategy will likely result in improved performance and higher rewards in future trials.
